<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelebs</span></b>  (not <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coelebs</span></b> ), lĭbis, adj.
		etym. dub., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>unmarried</i>, <i>single</i> (whether
			of a bachelor or a widower) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(censores) equitum peditumque prolem
					describunto: caelibes esse prohibento,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 3, 3, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 2, 4, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 5,
				10, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 5</span></i> Baumg.-Crus.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelebs senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Stich. 4, 1, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelebs quid agam Martiis Calendis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 8, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. S. 2, 5, 47</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 10,
				245</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 12, 63</span></i>; Gai
					<i><span class="en">Inst. 2, 286</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 1,
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 3, 34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vita,</span>”
				<i>the life of a bachelor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep 1, 1, 88</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 2, 163</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 5, 11, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					68, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 13,
			107</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of animals: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelebs aut vidua columba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 34, 52, § 104</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			trees to which no vine is attached (cf. marito): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caelebs platanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 15, 4</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14, 663</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 23, 35, § 204</span></i>
			.</div>
